================================================================================
Data / rule lists
================================================================================

- backend/src/services/germanAbbreviations.ts contains German + English
  abbreviation, unit, and symbol expansion rules inspired by
  repodiac/german_transliterate (CC-BY 4.0,
  https://github.com/repodiac/german_transliterate). Rules were
  reimplemented in TypeScript and extended with PageMentor-specific
  entries (Studienheft conventions, §§, Abb./Tab. formatting).

  Per CC-BY 4.0: copyright 2020 repodiac, licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International. See
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ for terms.
Embedding models (loaded into Ollama by the user, called over network
at runtime):
- jina-embeddings-v2-base-de  (Apache 2.0)
  https://huggingface.co/jinaai/jina-embeddings-v2-base-de
  preferred default for German study material — bilingual DE+EN,
  trained on German corpora, 768 dim, 8k context, ~440 MB.
- BGE-M3                      (MIT)
  https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-m3
  multilingual fallback for mixed-language libraries (100+ languages).
- nomic-embed-text            (Apache 2.0)
  https://huggingface.co/nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1
  last-resort fallback — smaller, English-focused.

